%% C4 level 4 (code): UML sequence diagram of accepting a significant change request
%% (SCRUM-70 AC10-AC11, SCRUM-44 A10). backend/app/events/routes.py: decide_change_request.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor COORD as Event Coordinator
    participant API as Event Workflow API
    participant RULES as Event Rules
    participant DM as Data Model
    participant DB as Database
    participant MQ as Message Broker

    COORD->>API: Accept change request
    API->>DB: Lock the event and the request
    API->>RULES: Parse decision: is the change significant?
    API->>DM: Apply new values to the event
    API->>DM: Flag affected venue bookings (never cancel)
    API->>RULES: Clear safety decision (Confirmed back to Approved)
    API->>DM: Notifications: organiser, and registered attendees if the times changed
    DM->>DM: before_flush: times changed, so release equipment reservations
    API->>DB: Commit all of the above together
    API->>MQ: Queue emails (after commit)
    API-->>COORD: 200, listing what was released and who was told
